handoff: Green 3.8: create only `harness/model-guide/review-score.ts`. Do not edit review-score.test.ts, the fixtures/review/ corpus, or plan.md. Read the doc comment at the top of review-score.test.ts as the binding contract. One recorded decision: test-strategy section 7 says the scorer is called in process, but this file pins a subprocess CLI, because FR-9 describes a command that writes the score file and every other tool in the phase is a CLI; no production export exists. If the orchestrator rules for an exported function, the CLI can call the same pure function. (1) CLI: `score --private <dir> --set <set_id> --route <route> --pass <n> --date <YYYY-MM-DD> --outputs <dir> --scores <dir> [--verdicts <file>]`. Each flag takes the next token as its value, so a trailing `--private` gives exit 2, stdout exactly `score: --private needs a value`, and no score file. (2) `--outputs` holds `<diff_id>.txt` for each key of the set; a missing file is an invalid review of that diff. (3) `--verdicts` is a flat JSON object `<diff_id>#F<n>` -> `real-defect` | `false-claim` | `unclear`; n is 1-based before the 30-finding cap; no entry is neutral. (4) Match: same `file`, line in `new_lines[0]-3` to `new_lines[1]+3`, class in `accepted_classes`; one finding to at most one plant, nearest plant range wins; a second finding on a found plant is a duplicate and neutral; only the first 30 findings of a diff count. No JSON block, invalid JSON, or a finding without `file` or `line` makes that diff invalid: `invalid_reviews` +1, and that diff has 0 found and 0 false claims. `false-claim` +1 to `false_claims`; `real-defect` +1 to `real_defects`; `unclear` sets the pass state `provisional`. (5) `W` is the weight sum of every plant of the set (132 here), `F` the found weight, `X` the false claims; score = `max(0, 100*F/W - 2*X)` rounded to one decimal; `blocker_recall = blockers_found / blockers` rounded to 4 decimals. (6) Pass record keys exactly `route, pass, date, state, score, weight, found_weight, found, missed, false_claims, blockers, blockers_found, blocker_recall, invalid_reviews, real_defects, by_class, by_severity`; `by_class` holds C1..C9 and `by_severity` holds blocker, major, minor, each `{found, missed}`. (7) Route record keys exactly `route, state, passes, worst, median, best, worst_blocker_recall, rank`; `state` is `complete` at 3 or more pass records (a provisional pass is complete) and `incomplete` below 3; `worst`/`best`/`median` are the pass scores, `worst_blocker_recall` is the lowest pass recall; rank complete routes by higher `worst`, then higher `worst_blocker_recall`, then higher `median`, 1-based; incomplete routes have `rank: null` and come last. (8) The score file `<scores>/<set_id>.json` holds exactly `set_id`, `passes`, `routes`; a run replaces a pass with the same route and pass number; it holds no `new_lines`, `witness`, `operator`, `file`, `line`, `title`, or `reason` key at any depth, no path, and no finding text. (9) Verify with `cd harness && npx vitest run model-guide-tests/review-score.test.ts --configLoader native --maxWorkers=1 --reporter=dot`; expect `Tests  19 passed (19)`. Run `git status --short docs/`; it must print nothing.
